.Dd 2026-06-04
.Dt NOMAD-ADOPT-DRIVE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-adopt-drive
.Nd adopt a plugged-in NOMAD library drive as this Mac's library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad adopt-drive
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad adopt-drive
makes a plugged-in
.Sy project-nomad
data drive the active library for this Mac, so its entire library
.Pq Information Library, Workshop, Maps, AI models
appears here.
It takes no arguments: it re-scans
.Pa /Volumes
for a single drive carrying a full
.Pa project-nomad/storage
library and adopts that one.
A drive that carries only AI models
.Pq no Pa storage No directory
is not adopted, because models already cross over to any Mac on their own.
.Pp
The command runs the following steps, and is idempotent
.Pq adopting the drive that is already active is a no-op :
.Bl -enum -width Ds
.It
Saves the current data root as
.Sy NOMAD_PREV_DATA_ROOT
so the library can be restored automatically when the drive is ejected.
.It
Re-points
.Sy NOMAD_DATA_ROOT
to the drive's
.Pa project-nomad
path.
.It
Restarts the content stack
.Pq Ic docker compose up -d --force-recreate
so the containers re-bind to the drive's
.Pa storage
directory.
.It
Waits for the admin service to come back up against the new data root.
.It
Reconciles the catalog to the drive's files
.Pq see Xr nomad-reconcile 1 ,
so the Workshop, Information Library, Maps, and models all surface.
.El
.Pp
Only one data root is active at a time, so adopting a drive replaces the
previous library for as long as the drive stays plugged in.
Eject the drive and this Mac reverts to its own library automatically.
The drive's catalog
.Pq MySQL
stays on this Mac's internal disk; the drive carries the files, which is why
the reconcile step is needed.
.Pp
This command is also exposed in the Command Center as the
.Dq Adopt this drive
button, which runs it on the host through the host-command bridge.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad adopt-drive
Adopt the single plugged-in NOMAD library drive and surface its full library.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-reconcile 1 ,
.Xr nomad-up 1
